Owlbears.

Yes, I know: projectile weapons or attack wands.

Suppose you haven't got any of that.  Let's say your role is
restricted to unskilled in dagger, so you've been leaving those
behind, and what few darts you happened upon earlier have long since
been thrown and lost.  You've got wands, but they're not attack
wands:  probing and digging (but down leads to the big room) and
something else equally non-damaging, maybe one of the ones that makes
engravings vanish or slows down the bugs on the floor, something like
that.  Nothing that's going to kill an owlbear.

You can evade the owlbears somewhat, by just plain going in the other
direction, but at some point the RNG decides there should be more than
one owlbear, so you get into a situation where going back the other
way would mean facing the other one...

Here's the ttyrec:
http://alt.org/nethack/userdata/J/Jonadab/ttyrec/2011-11-30.22:07:29.ttyrec
Fast-forward until you see the Big Room.  (That's when I realized my
initial tactic of sneaking past the owlbears had backfired, because I
needed to get back past them again...)

I know full well that I shouldn't have tried to hit it in melee.  I
was frustrated and not thinking clearly, and, as a new player, I'm
still working on developing my sense of how advanced my character
needs to be before I *can* pull stunts like that.  In this case I
suspected it would get me killed, but I couldn't think of anything
else to try.  Going back down would have just taken me to the other
owlbear and, if I slipped past that again, to the Big Room.

So what *should* I have done?

Should I have zapped the wand that makes engravings vanish at the
owlbear, in hopes that maybe it would be teleport and I could at least
get past it for the time being?  (Hmm...  on closer review the third
wand was slow monster.  Would that have helped at all?  I mean, if the
owlbear crushes me to death slowly, is that more beneficial somehow?)

Did I have any other options?


